messages:   11%|#         | 64/600 [00:36<06:37,  1.35it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe prehistoric fish Tiktaalik is the earliest known animal with fingers. Since variations were so great among prehistoric fish species, Tiktaalik would not have stood out as unusual at the time. However, Tiktaalik' s fingers were an important development in animal evolution because it is likely that Tiktaalik is an ancestor to the many land animals with fingers.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, the statements above, if true, most strongly support which one of the following?\n# Options:\nA) Tiktaalik is not the ancestor of any currently surviving fish species.\nB) Tiktaalik's fingers were its only feature to play a significant role in the development of modern land animals.\nC) The evolutionary significance of tiktaalik could not be determined just through comparison to fish species of its time.\nD) No fish without fingers would ever be able to move on land.", "To solve this logical reasoning problem, let's carefully analyze the context and the question, and then evaluate each option.\n\n### Context Analysis:.\n1.**Tiktaalik is the earliest known animal with fingers.**.\n2.**Variations among prehistoric fish species were great.**.\n3.**Tiktaalik's fingers were an important development in animal evolution.**.\n4.**Tiktaalik is likely an ancestor to many land animals with fingers.**.\n\n### Question:.Based on the above information, the statements above, if true, least strongly support which one of the following?. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
