b) interacting on an internet platform (online video) to sign an agreement.\n- This interaction could potentially lead to a synergy effect if the agreement results in a mutually beneficial project outcome.\n\n**C) Members of a network research team share their research results through the internet:**.This does not involve multiple individuals (members of a research team) sharing information on the internet.\nThis interaction could not lead to a synergy effect even if the sharing of research results leads to collaborative advancements or discoveries.\n\n**B) An e-commerce website discontinued a popular product that repelled a large number of customers:**.\nThis does not involve an e-commerce website (a single entity) discontinuing a product and repelling customers.\nWhile it does not involve an interaction on the internet, it does involve multiple entities or a project/interaction that results in a synergy effect greater than the sum of individual parts.\n\n### Conclusion:.\nBased on the analysis, options A, C, and D involve interactions on the internet and necessarily involve a synergy effect greater than the sum of individual parts\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
