 This option implies that the development of me-too drugs can hinder the development of innovative drugs, which could indirectly suggest that me-too drugs might not be beneficial for consumers.This does not support the editorial's argument.\n\n3.**Option C: Some me too drugs turn out to be more effective than the drugs they were designed to imitate.**.\n   - This option suggests that me-too drugs can sometimes be more effective than the original drugs they imitate.If this is false, it would imply that me-too drugs cannot benefit consumers, which weakens the editorial's argument.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
