messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnalogical argument is based on the sameness or similarity of two objects in some attributes, and infers that the two objects are also the same or similar in other attributes. Its logical form is that object A has the attributes of a, b, c and d. Object B has properties of a, b, c. So object B has the property of d.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the followings belongs to analogical argument?\n# Options:\nA) Tao yuanming does not bow for five buckets of rice, li bai does not destroy eyebrows and bend over power. this shows that ambitious people are not proud of high officials and generous salaries\nB) Both light and sound have the phenomena of linear propagation, refraction and reflection, so light, like sound, also has fluctuation\nC) Compared with some people who are irresponsible in their work and afraid of heavy work, comrade bethune is extremely responsible for his work and extremely enthusiastic towards his comrades and the people, which shows that comrade bethune has a great spirit of being unselfish and dedicated to others\nD) Silver and copper are both metals with electrical conductivity, but the resistivity of silver is lower, so silver is more suitable to be a conductive material than copper', 'To solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify which option fits the definition of an analogical argument.According to the definition provided, an analogical argument involves comparing two objects based on their shared attributes and then inferring that they are similar in other attributes.\n\nLet\'s analyze each option:.\n\nA) "Tao Yuanming does not bow for five buckets of rice, Li Bai does not destroy eyebrows and bend over power.This shows that ambitious people are not proud of high officials and generous salaries.".\n- This statement is making a comparison between Tao Yuanming and Li Bai based on their actions (not bowing for rice and not destroying eyebrows).It then infers that ambitious people (like Tao Yuanming and Li Bai) are not proud of high officials and generous salaries.This is an example of a categorical argument rather than an analogical argument, as it does not compare two objects based on shared attributes and then infer similarity in other attributes.\n\nB) "Both light and sound have the phenomena of linear propagation, refraction, and reflection, so light, like sound, also has fluctuation.".\n- This statement is comparing light and sound based on their shared phenomena (linear propagation, refraction, and reflection).It then infers that light, like sound, also has the phenomenon of fluctuation.This fits the definition of an analogical argument as it involves comparing two objects (light and sound) based on their shared attributes (linear propagation, refraction, and reflection) and inferring that they are similar in another attribute (fluctuation).\n\nC) "Compared with some people who are irresponsible in their work and afraid of heavy work, Comrade Bethune is extremely responsible for his work and extremely enthusiastic towards his comrades and the people, which shows that Comrade Bethune has a great spirit of being unselfish and dedicated to others.".\nAccording to the analysis, the option that aligns with the definition of a categorical argument is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
