messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nInvisible curriculum refers to the informal and unconscious learning experience that is not clearly specified in the school's planned curriculum.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following is not an invisible curriculum?\n# Options:\nA) Colleges and universities organize students to participate in two-day military training to cultivate and exercise students' willpower.\nB) When children learn teaching courses, they cultivate their interest in learning and teaching.\nC) A university set up a university culture festival to let students know the school motto and style of study.\nD) Teachers and students participate in extracurricular activities together to establish an equal and harmonious relationship between teachers and students.", 'To solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify which option does not align with the definition of an "invisible curriculum."According to the definition, an invisible curriculum is informal and unconscious learning that is not clearly specified in the school\'s planned curriculum.\n\nLet\'s analyze each option:.\n\nA) Colleges and universities organize students to participate in two-day military training to cultivate and exercise students\' willpower.\n- This option describes a structured, organized activity (two-day military training) that is part of the planned curriculum.Therefore, it is not an example of an invisible curriculum.\n\nB) When children learn teaching courses, they cultivate their interest in learning and teaching.\n- This option describes a specific course (teaching courses) that is part of the planned curriculum.Thus, it is not an example of an invisible curriculum.\n\nC) A university set up a university culture festival to let students know the school motto and style of study.\n- This option describes an informal, unplanned activity (extracurricular activities) that is not part of the planned curriculum. This does not fit the definition of an invisible curriculum.\n\nD) Teachers and students do not participate in extracurricular activities together to establish an equal and harmonious relationship between teachers and students.\n- This option describes a festival that is part of the planned university culture and curriculum. Therefore, it is an example of an invisible curriculum.\n\nBased on the analysis, the option that is not an example of an invisible curriculum is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
