messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nBroken window effect is a psychological phenomenon, that is, if the window of a house is broken and no one repair it, and soon other windows will also be broken.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which one of the followings does not belong to broken window effect?\n# Options:\nA) If the graffiti on a wall is not cleaned, the wall will soon be full of messy and ugly things.\nB) If a tributary is polluted and not treated, it may pollute the water quality of the whole basin.\nC) Once there is rubbish in a very clean place, people will throw their rubbish away without hesitation and will not feel ashamed.\nD) If a few people in a group speak uncivilized languages and are not stopped, many people will soon speak uncivilized languages.', "To solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to understand the broken window effect and apply it to each of the given options.The broken window effect suggests that if a small problem (like a broken window) is not addressed, it will lead to more problems (like more broken windows).\n\nLet's analyze each option:.\n\nA) If the graffiti on a wall is not cleaned, the wall will soon be full of messy and ugly things.\n- This fits the broken window effect.If graffiti is not cleaned, it will likely lead to more graffiti being added to the wall.\n\nB) If a tributary is polluted and not treated, it may pollute the water quality of the whole basin.\n- This also fits the broken window effect.If pollution is not treated, it can spread and affect the entire basin.\n\nC) Once there is rubbish in a very clean place, people will throw their rubbish away without hesitation and will not feel ashamed.\n- This does not fit the broken window effect.In this scenario, the presence of rubbish does not lead to more rubbish being added.On the contrary, it indicates that the initial presence of rubbish could result in a change in behavior, leading to a chain reaction of more rubbish being added.\n\nB) If a few people in a group speak uncivilized languages and are not stopped, many people will soon speak uncivilized languages.\n- This aligns with the broken window effect.If a few people speak uncivilized languages and are not stopped, it will likely lead to more people speaking uncivilized languages.\n\nConsidering the evaluation, option B does fit the broken window effect as depicted.\n\nHence, the accurate answer is:\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
