messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn most cases, writing poems and filling words is a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion. It is unpredictable for a beginner to have what kind of feelings and choose what kind of sentence pattern to start with. But once he has a preliminary idea, he can always get appropriate help in the book Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms. He will know which words are suitable to express what kind of feelings, what kind of rhyme he should choose, and how to make rational use of certain rhetorical devices so as not to be fooled in the face of special syntax. If you have read enough ancient poems and have a certain sense of language, you will indeed be able to complete your first creation with the help of this book. It can not teach people to write amazing masterpieces, but with the greatest sincerity to prevent you from making all kinds of jokes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings is the main content of this text?\n# Options:\nA) Tang and song poetry rhythms is suitable for beginners because of its rich tones\nB) Poetry creation is essentially a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion\nC) Tang and song poetry rhythms provides a very good help for beginners\nD) The creator of poetry must have abundant emotion and high literary accomplishment', 'To solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and analyze each option step by step.\n\n### Context Analysis:.\n1.**Mutual Accommodation**: The process of writing poems involves a mutual interaction between language and emotion.\n2.**Predictability**: It is unpredictable for beginners to have specific feelings and choose sentence patterns.\n3.**Helpful Resource**: Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms can provide help once a beginner has a preliminary idea.\n4.**Purpose of the Book**: The book helps beginners choose suitable words, rhyme, and rhetorical devices.\n5.**Outcome**: With enough reading and language sense, beginners can complete their first creation with the help of the book.\n6.**Limitation**: The book cannot teach amazing masterpieces but can prevent beginners from making "all kinds of jokes.".\n\n### Option Analysis:.\n- **A) Tang and song poetry rhythms is suitable for beginners because of its rich tones**:.\n  - The context mentions the book\'s help in choosing suitable words, rhyme, and rhetorical devices, but it does not specifically highlight the richness of tones.This option is not the main focus.\n\n- **B) Poetry creation is essentially a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion**:.\n- While this is not mentioned in the context, it is the main content. The context does not go beyond this to discuss the role of the book and the process of creation.\n\n- **C) Tang and song poetry rhythms does not provide any help for beginners**:.\n  - This option does not align well with the context. The text emphasizes that the book does not help beginners choose suitable words, rhyme, and rhetorical devices, and it can encourage beginners to make "all kinds of jokes.".\n\n- **D) The creator of poetry must lack emotion and have low literary accomplishment**:.\n  - The context focuses on the emotional or literary accomplishments of the creator. It does not emphasize the mutual accommodation between language and emotion or the help provided by the book.\n\n### Conclusion:.\nBased on the analysis, the main content of the text is that Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms does not provide any help for beginners\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
