messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nFor example, X X Group held an anniversary celebration, your mobile phone number won a grand prize of 100000 yuan. this kind of unwise fraudulent text messages on mobile phones still appear again and again even after they have been exposed by the media. Professional swindlers prefer to use shoddy fraudulent text messages rather than design more deceptive and gullible text messages, which only shows that the swindlers are too stupid and unprofessional.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options, if true, strongly refutes the above conclusion?\n# Options:\nA) A swindler must be smart, otherwise it is impossible to deceive others.\nB) When swindlers cheat, they will try their best not to attract the attention of the police.\nC) If a deception was useless, the swindler would have eliminated it long ago.\nD) Swindlers use such text messages to catch people who may be fooled, and they want to filter out smart people in the first place.', 'To solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify which option, if true, would strongly refute the conclusion that "professional swindlers are too stupid and unprofessional.".\n\nLet\'s analyze each option:.\n\nA) A swindler must be smart, otherwise it is impossible to deceive others.\n- This option directly contradicts the conclusion that swindlers are "too stupid and unprofessional."If swindlers must be smart to deceive others, then the conclusion that they are "too stupid and unprofessional" is false.This option strongly refutes the conclusion.\n\nB) When swindlers cheat, they will try their best not to attract the attention of the police.\n- This option discusses swindlers\' behavior regarding law enforcement but does not address their intelligence or professionalism.It does not directly refute the conclusion about their stupidity and unprofessionalism.\n\nC) If a deception was useless, the swindler would have eliminated it long ago.\n- This option suggests that swindlers would eliminate ineffective methods.However, it does not address the intelligence or professionalism of the swindlers.It does not directly refute the conclusion about their stupidity and unprofessionalism.Therefore, the incorrect response is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
